&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;This is part 2 of 8 of the free series &lt;a href="https://tt-tech.io/series/frontend-system-design" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;Frontend system design for enterprise applications&lt;/a&gt;, first published on &lt;a href="https://tt-tech.io/blog/enterprise-frontend-state-ownership" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;tt-tech.io&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;A support agent opens the link a customer sent: an account page, filtered on one category. The page shows all categories, because the filter lived in a component field and not in the URL. Nobody wrote a bug. The state was stored as the wrong kind.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;That is the state problem in enterprise apps. The library choice comes last. First you decide what kind each piece of state is, who owns it, and how long it lives.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  Five kinds of state
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Server data.&lt;/strong&gt; Accounts, transactions. The backend owns it; the frontend holds a copy that can be stale (part 3).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;UI state.&lt;/strong&gt; Which panel is open. Owned by one component, gone when it is gone.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Form state.&lt;/strong&gt; A draft, its validation, whether it is dirty.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;URL state.&lt;/strong&gt; Filters, tabs, the selected record. Anything a link, a support ticket or the back button must restore.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Session state.&lt;/strong&gt; The user and their roles. Truly global.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;A common state bug is one kind stored as another: server data copied into a component, a filter in memory that belongs in the URL, roles cached in a store nobody refreshes.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://media2.dev.to/dynamic/image/width=800%2Cheight=%2Cfit=scale-down%2Cgravity=auto/https%3A%2F%2Fdev-to-uploads.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com%2Fuploads%2Farticles%2F48ffean7v511fa2fsdds.webp" class="article-body-image-wrapper"&gt;&lt;img src="https://media2.dev.to/dynamic/image/width=800%2Cheight=%2Cfit=scale-down%2Cgravity=auto/https%3A%2F%2Fdev-to-uploads.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com%2Fuploads%2Farticles%2F48ffean7v511fa2fsdds.webp" alt="Five kinds of state, each with an example on Atlas Bank, its owner, where it lives and how long: server data such as accounts lives in AccountsStore until it is stale; UI state lives in a component signal until the component is gone; form state lives in the form model until submit or cancel; URL state such as the account id and the filter lives in the URL as long as the link; session state, the user and their roles, lives in one global store until logout. A common bug is one kind stored as another" width="799" height="358"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  The URL is state
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;If a person might share it, bookmark it or go back to it, it belongs in the URL. In Angular, &lt;code&gt;withComponentInputBinding&lt;/code&gt; binds route parameters to component inputs, and by default the router sets an input to &lt;code&gt;undefined&lt;/code&gt; when the value is missing from the route, which "ensures that stale data is not retained".&lt;a href="https://angular.dev/guide/routing/common-router-tasks" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;[1]&lt;/a&gt; Query parameters bind the same way, so a filter can live there too.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  One store per domain, one global store at most
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;I would give each domain its own store: accounts, cards, requests. A team owns its store the way it owns its library. A single global store looks tidy on day one and turns into the place where every team's state meets every other team's bugs.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;What stays global is what is cross-cutting by nature: the session, the permissions, maybe feature flags. Everything else stays close to the feature that owns it.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  Derive, do not duplicate
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;A total balance is not state. It is a function of the accounts. Angular says it directly: "Avoid using effects for propagation of state changes", use computed signals instead.&lt;a href="https://angular.dev/guide/signals/effect" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;[2]&lt;/a&gt; React says the same in its own words: "When something can be calculated from the existing props or state, don't put it in state. Instead, calculate it during rendering."&lt;a href="https://react.dev/learn/you-might-not-need-an-effect" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;[3]&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://media2.dev.to/dynamic/image/width=800%2Cheight=%2Cfit=scale-down%2Cgravity=auto/https%3A%2F%2Fdev-to-uploads.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com%2Fuploads%2Farticles%2Fcuvdjk541qsb2m7e4xm1.webp" class="article-body-image-wrapper"&gt;&lt;img src="https://media2.dev.to/dynamic/image/width=800%2Cheight=%2Cfit=scale-down%2Cgravity=auto/https%3A%2F%2Fdev-to-uploads.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com%2Fuploads%2Farticles%2Fcuvdjk541qsb2m7e4xm1.webp" alt="Derived against duplicated. Two open accounts of 12 400,00 MAD and 30 000,00 MAD give a total balance of 42 400,00 MAD. After a transfer of 500,00 MAD, the derived total, a computed signal, follows to 41 900,00 MAD and every screen shows the same number. A duplicated total, set once or by an effect, stays at 42 400,00 MAD, so two owners disagree" width="800" height="358"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;blockquote&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Every copy of a value is a second owner. Two owners will disagree.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/blockquote&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  Long regulated forms
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;A loan application or a patient intake form is state with rules: drafts that survive a lunch break, validation that mirrors the server's, and dirty tracking so nobody loses an hour of input. The server still validates; the client check is for the person typing.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;For new code, Angular's Signal Forms sync the form model with its fields automatically. The Angular team is careful here: they "work best in new applications built with signals", and "reactive forms remain a solid choice" in an existing app that uses them.&lt;a href="https://angular.dev/guide/forms/signals/overview" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;[4]&lt;/a&gt; In a ten-year codebase, that is the right advice. Do not migrate forms for fashion.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  Signals or RxJS
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;My rule: signals for state (a value now), RxJS for events over time (keystrokes, websockets, retries). The bridge exists: &lt;code&gt;toSignal&lt;/code&gt; turns an Observable into a signal and "behaves similarly to the async pipe in templates".&lt;a href="https://angular.dev/ecosystem/rxjs-interop" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;[5]&lt;/a&gt; Signals also fit zoneless Angular, where "updating a signal that's read in a template" is one of the notifications that schedules change detection.&lt;a href="https://angular.dev/guide/zoneless" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;[6]&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  On Atlas Bank
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;code&gt;AccountsStore&lt;/code&gt; in &lt;code&gt;libs/data-access/banking&lt;/code&gt; keeps its state private and hands out read-only signals and derived values:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight typescript"&gt;&lt;code&gt;  &lt;span class="k"&gt;private&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;readonly&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;accountsState&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;signal&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="k"&gt;readonly&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nc"&gt;Account&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;]&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;]&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="k"&gt;private&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;readonly&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;transactionsState&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;signal&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="k"&gt;readonly&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nc"&gt;Transaction&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;]&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;]&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="k"&gt;private&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;readonly&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;beneficiariesState&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;signal&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="k"&gt;readonly&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nc"&gt;Beneficiary&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;]&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;]&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="k"&gt;private&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;readonly&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;loadingState&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;signal&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="kc"&gt;false&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="k"&gt;private&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;readonly&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;loadedState&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;signal&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="kc"&gt;false&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="k"&gt;private&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;inFlight&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;?:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nb"&gt;Promise&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="k"&gt;void&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;

  &lt;span class="k"&gt;readonly&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;accounts&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kc"&gt;this&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;accountsState&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;asReadonly&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="k"&gt;readonly&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;transactions&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kc"&gt;this&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;transactionsState&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;asReadonly&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="k"&gt;readonly&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;beneficiaries&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kc"&gt;this&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;beneficiariesState&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;asReadonly&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="k"&gt;readonly&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;loading&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kc"&gt;this&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;loadingState&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;asReadonly&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="k"&gt;readonly&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;loaded&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kc"&gt;this&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;loadedState&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;asReadonly&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;

  &lt;span class="k"&gt;readonly&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;totalBalanceMad&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;computed&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="kc"&gt;this&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;accountsState&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;
      &lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;filter&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;a&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;a&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;status&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;!==&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s1"&gt;'closed'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;
      &lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;reduce&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;sum&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;a&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;sum&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;+&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;a&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;balanceMad&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="mi"&gt;0&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;&lt;code&gt;asReadonly()&lt;/code&gt; exposes a value "without allowing them to modify it directly",&lt;a href="https://angular.dev/guide/signals" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;[7]&lt;/a&gt; so the store is the only owner. The account detail page gets its &lt;code&gt;id&lt;/code&gt; from the route through &lt;code&gt;withComponentInputBinding&lt;/code&gt; and derives the filtered list with &lt;code&gt;computed&lt;/code&gt;. Its category filter, though, is a component signal. Fine for a demo; in a bank's support flow I would move it to a query parameter.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The legacy transfer screen shows the old shape: plain fields, manual subscriptions, and &lt;code&gt;markForCheck()&lt;/code&gt; after them. The repo's &lt;code&gt;AGENTS.md&lt;/code&gt; calls that "a smell to migrate, not a pattern to copy".&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  What I left out, and why
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Redux, MobX, Zustand, NgRx comparisons.&lt;/strong&gt; A library tour. Ownership decides first; any of them can hold the result.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Immutability as a concept.&lt;/strong&gt; Implied by read-only signals and derived values.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Event sourcing on the client.&lt;/strong&gt; Rare in a frontend, a backend shape.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Atomic state.&lt;/strong&gt; React library vocabulary for the same idea as "derive, do not duplicate".&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  On Monday
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Pick one screen and label every piece of state with its kind: server, UI, form, URL, session.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Find one value stored twice. Make one of them a &lt;code&gt;computed&lt;/code&gt; (or a calculation during render).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Find one filter that a support ticket cannot reproduce. Move it to the URL.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://tt-tech.io/blog/enterprise-frontend-networking-caching" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;Part 3, on networking and caching&lt;/a&gt;, is next.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  For your coding agent
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The rules of this article, written for an agent. Paste them into your &lt;code&gt;AGENTS.md&lt;/code&gt;, save them as a skill, or point your agent at the file.&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight markdown"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="gu"&gt;# State rules for enterprise apps
&lt;/span&gt;
Source: https://tt-tech.io/blog/enterprise-frontend-state-ownership
For Angular and React frontends. Add to AGENTS.md or save as a skill. Your project's own rules win where they differ.

&lt;span class="gu"&gt;## Rules
&lt;/span&gt;
1. Before you add state, name its kind: server data, UI state, form state, URL state or session state. Store it as that kind.
2. Put anything a link, a bookmark, a support ticket or the back button must restore in the URL: filters, tabs, the selected record. In Angular, bind route and query parameters to inputs with &lt;span class="sb"&gt;`withComponentInputBinding`&lt;/span&gt;, and expect a missing parameter to arrive as &lt;span class="sb"&gt;`undefined`&lt;/span&gt;.
3. Server data belongs to the backend. Never copy it into a component. Read it from the store of its domain.
4. Give each domain its own store (accounts, cards, requests), owned by the team that owns the domain. Never add a single global store for everything.
5. Keep global only what is cross-cutting by nature: the session, the permissions, maybe feature flags. Do not cache roles in a store nobody refreshes.
6. Keep UI state (which panel is open) in the component that owns it.
7. Derive, do not duplicate. If a value can be calculated from state, use &lt;span class="sb"&gt;`computed`&lt;/span&gt; in Angular or calculate it during render in React. Never store it as a second copy.
8. Never use &lt;span class="sb"&gt;`effect`&lt;/span&gt; to propagate state changes. Use &lt;span class="sb"&gt;`computed`&lt;/span&gt; instead.
9. Keep a store's writable state private. Expose read-only signals with &lt;span class="sb"&gt;`asReadonly()`&lt;/span&gt; and derived values, so the store is the only owner.
10. In long regulated forms, keep drafts, mirror the server's validation and track dirty state. The server still validates; the client check is for the person typing.
11. Use Signal Forms in new code built with signals. Keep reactive forms in an existing app that uses them. Do not migrate forms for fashion.
12. Use signals for state (a value now) and RxJS for events over time (keystrokes, websockets, retries). Bridge them with &lt;span class="sb"&gt;`toSignal`&lt;/span&gt;.

&lt;span class="gu"&gt;## Before you say done
&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;- &lt;/span&gt;For every new piece of state in the diff, list its kind and its owner in the pull request.
&lt;span class="k"&gt;- &lt;/span&gt;Search the diff for &lt;span class="sb"&gt;`effect(`&lt;/span&gt; calls that set other state, and for stored values that could be a &lt;span class="sb"&gt;`computed`&lt;/span&gt; or a calculation during render.
&lt;span class="k"&gt;- &lt;/span&gt;For every new filter, tab or selection, confirm it lives in the URL, or say why not.
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;The same rules as a file: &lt;a href="https://tt-tech.io/agents/enterprise-frontend-state-ownership.md" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;https://tt-tech.io/agents/enterprise-frontend-state-ownership.md&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  Sources
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;ol&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Angular, &lt;a href="https://angular.dev/guide/routing/common-router-tasks" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;Other routing tasks&lt;/a&gt;, docs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Angular, &lt;a href="https://angular.dev/guide/signals/effect" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;Side effects for non-reactives APIs&lt;/a&gt;, docs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;React, &lt;a href="https://react.dev/learn/you-might-not-need-an-effect" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;You Might Not Need an Effect&lt;/a&gt;, docs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Angular, &lt;a href="https://angular.dev/guide/forms/signals/overview" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;Forms with Angular Signals&lt;/a&gt;, docs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Angular, &lt;a href="https://angular.dev/ecosystem/rxjs-interop" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;RxJS interop with Angular signals&lt;/a&gt;, docs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Angular, &lt;a href="https://angular.dev/guide/zoneless" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;Angular without ZoneJS (Zoneless)&lt;/a&gt;, docs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Angular, &lt;a href="https://angular.dev/guide/signals" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;Angular Signals&lt;/a&gt;, docs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;




&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Part 2 of 8 of the free series &lt;a href="https://tt-tech.io/series/frontend-system-design" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;Frontend system design for enterprise applications&lt;/a&gt; on tt-tech.io, also in French and Arabic.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Have you ever noticed how some websites reveal their content gradually as you scroll down the page?&lt;br&gt;
Instead of displaying all elements at once, headings, buttons, images, and other elements appear with smooth animations.&lt;br&gt;
This technique is often called Staggered Animations.&lt;br&gt;
In this tutorial, I'll show you how to create this effect in a React application using a lightweight JavaScript library called AOS (Animate On Scroll).&lt;br&gt;
I'll use a real example from my Cosmetics website to demonstrate how different elements can appear with different animation delays.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What Is AOS?&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;AOS stands for Animate On Scroll.&lt;br&gt;
It's a JavaScript library that allows developers to animate elements when they enter the viewport.&lt;br&gt;
Instead of implementing custom scroll event listeners, we can simply add HTML data attributes to the elements we want to animate.&lt;br&gt;
For example:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight jsx"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;jsx&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;h1&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;data&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;-&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;aos&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;"fade-up"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="nc"&gt;Welcome&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;to&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nc"&gt;Our&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nc"&gt;Website&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;h1&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;


&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;This makes the heading appear with a fade-up animation when it enters the viewport.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Installing AOS in React&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;First, install the library:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight shell"&gt;&lt;code&gt;bash
npm install aos
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;Next, import AOS and its CSS file into your React application:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight jsx"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;jsx&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;import&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nc"&gt;React&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;useEffect&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;from&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s1"&gt;'react'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;import&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nc"&gt;Aos&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;from&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s1"&gt;'aos'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;import&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s1"&gt;'aos/dist/aos.css'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;Then initialize the library inside your main component:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight jsx"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;jsx&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nf"&gt;useEffect&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="nc"&gt;Aos&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;init&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="n"&gt;duration&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="mi"&gt;1000&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;]&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;Let's understand the configuration:&lt;br&gt;
duration: 1000 sets the animation duration to 1000 milliseconds.&lt;br&gt;
Aos.init() initializes the animation library.&lt;br&gt;
useEffect() runs the initialization after the component mounts.&lt;br&gt;
[] ensures the effect runs only once per mount.&lt;br&gt;
Now AOS is ready to use throughout the application.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Understanding Staggered Animations&lt;/strong&gt; &lt;br&gt;
One interesting feature of AOS is the ability to control when individual elements start their animations.&lt;br&gt;
We can achieve this using:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight jsx"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;jsx&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="n"&gt;data&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;-&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;aos&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;-&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;delay&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;"500"&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;The delay value is measured in milliseconds.&lt;br&gt;
For example:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight jsx"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;jsx&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;div&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;data&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;-&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;aos&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;"fade-up"&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;data&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;-&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;aos&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;-&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;delay&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;"200"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="nc"&gt;First&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nc"&gt;Element&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;div&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;div&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;data&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;-&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;aos&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;"fade-up"&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;data&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;-&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;aos&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;-&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;delay&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;"400"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="nc"&gt;Second&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nc"&gt;Element&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;div&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;div&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;data&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;-&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;aos&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;"fade-up"&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;data&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;-&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;aos&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;-&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;delay&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;"600"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="nc"&gt;Third&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nc"&gt;Element&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;div&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;Each element has the same animation, but a different delay.&lt;br&gt;
This creates a sequential visual effect rather than making all elements animate simultaneously.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;A Real Example from My React Project&lt;/strong&gt; &lt;br&gt;
In my Cosmetics website, I used this technique inside the Hero section.&lt;br&gt;
The goal was to make the content appear gradually and create a more engaging first impression.&lt;br&gt;
Here is a simplified version of the implementation:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight jsx"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;jsx&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="kd"&gt;function&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nc"&gt;Hero&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="k"&gt;return&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;section&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;

      &lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;hgroup&lt;/span&gt;
        &lt;span class="n"&gt;data&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;-&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;aos&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;"fade-up"&lt;/span&gt;
        &lt;span class="n"&gt;data&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;-&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;aos&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;-&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;delay&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;"500"&lt;/span&gt;
      &lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
        &lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;h1&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
          &lt;span class="nc"&gt;Enhance&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nc"&gt;Your&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nc"&gt;Natural&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nc"&gt;Beauty&lt;/span&gt;
        &lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;h1&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;

        &lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;p&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
          &lt;span class="nc"&gt;Discover&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;beauty&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="ow"&gt;and&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;skincare&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;treatments&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;
        &lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;p&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
      &lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;hgroup&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;

      &lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;nav&lt;/span&gt;
        &lt;span class="n"&gt;data&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;-&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;aos&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;"fade-up"&lt;/span&gt;
        &lt;span class="n"&gt;data&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;-&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;aos&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;-&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;delay&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;"600"&lt;/span&gt;
      &lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
        &lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;a&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;href&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;"#appointment"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
          &lt;span class="nc"&gt;Book&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;a&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nc"&gt;Consultation&lt;/span&gt;
        &lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;a&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;

        &lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;a&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;href&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;"#services"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
          &lt;span class="nc"&gt;Explore&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nc"&gt;Services&lt;/span&gt;
        &lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;a&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
      &lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;nav&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;

      &lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;aside&lt;/span&gt;
        &lt;span class="n"&gt;data&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;-&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;aos&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;"fade-up"&lt;/span&gt;
        &lt;span class="n"&gt;data&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;-&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;aos&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;-&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;delay&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;"800"&lt;/span&gt;
      &lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
        &lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;p&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="mi"&gt;2&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="mi"&gt;500&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;+&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nc"&gt;Happy&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nc"&gt;Clients&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;p&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
        &lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;p&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="mi"&gt;15&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;+&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nc"&gt;Specialists&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;p&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
        &lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;p&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="mi"&gt;50&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;+&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nc"&gt;Treatments&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;p&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
        &lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;p&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="mi"&gt;10&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;+&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nc"&gt;Years&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;p&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
      &lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;aside&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;

      &lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;figure&lt;/span&gt;
        &lt;span class="n"&gt;data&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;-&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;aos&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;"fade-up"&lt;/span&gt;
        &lt;span class="n"&gt;data&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;-&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;aos&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;-&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;delay&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;"700"&lt;/span&gt;
      &lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
        &lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;img&lt;/span&gt;
          &lt;span class="n"&gt;src&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;"/images/hero.png"&lt;/span&gt;
          &lt;span class="n"&gt;alt&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;"Cosmetic treatment"&lt;/span&gt;
        &lt;span class="o"&gt;/&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
      &lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;figure&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;

    &lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;section&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;Notice that I didn't apply the animation to every individual element.&lt;br&gt;
Instead, I applied it to groups of related elements using semantic HTML elements such as hgroup, nav, aside, and figure.&lt;br&gt;
This keeps the JSX cleaner and makes the animation behavior easier to manage.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Analyzing the Animation Delays&lt;/strong&gt; &lt;br&gt;
Let's look at the actual delay values used in my project:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Heading &amp;amp; Description: fade-up — 500ms&lt;br&gt;
Navigation Buttons: fade-up — 600ms&lt;br&gt;
Hero Image: fade-up — 700ms&lt;br&gt;
Statistics: fade-up — 800ms&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;All four elements use the same animation, but their delays create a layered visual experience.&lt;br&gt;
One important detail: the delays are relative to when each element's animation is triggered, so the actual appearance sequence can also depend on when each element enters the viewport.&lt;br&gt;
This gives developers more control over how content is revealed while scrolling.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Other Animation Effects You Can Use&lt;/strong&gt; &lt;br&gt;
AOS provides several animation types beyond fade-up.&lt;br&gt;
Here are a few examples:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight jsx"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;jsx&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;div&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;data&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;-&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;aos&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;"fade-up"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="nc"&gt;Fade&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nc"&gt;Up&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;div&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;div&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;data&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;-&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;aos&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;"fade-right"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="nc"&gt;Fade&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nc"&gt;Right&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;div&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;div&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;data&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;-&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;aos&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;"zoom-in"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="nc"&gt;Zoom&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nc"&gt;In&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;div&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;div&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;data&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;-&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;aos&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;"flip-left"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="nc"&gt;Flip&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nc"&gt;Left&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;div&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;You can experiment with different effects depending on the design of your website.&lt;br&gt;
For example, fade animations work well for text, while zoom animations can be useful for images and visual cards.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Some Tips from My Experience&lt;/strong&gt; &lt;br&gt;
After working with AOS in my React project, here are a few things I recommend:&lt;br&gt;
Don't animate every element. Too many animations can make the interface distracting.&lt;br&gt;
Use delays carefully to create a natural visual flow.&lt;br&gt;
Keep animation durations reasonable.&lt;br&gt;
Test your animations on mobile devices.&lt;br&gt;
Consider users who prefer reduced motion.&lt;br&gt;
Animations should improve the user experience, not slow down the interaction.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Final Thoughts&lt;/strong&gt; &lt;br&gt;
Adding scroll animations to a React application doesn't have to be complicated.&lt;br&gt;
With AOS, we can create engaging visual effects using simple data attributes without writing custom scroll detection logic.&lt;br&gt;
The most interesting part is not simply adding animations, but controlling their timing to create a more natural and enjoyable browsing experience.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Do you prefer using animation libraries like AOS, or do you prefer implementing animations with CSS?&lt;br&gt;
Share your thoughts in the comments!&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Microsoft Publisher is being discontinued at the end of October 2026. For years I used it for a hobby: designing transit network maps, the kind with colored lines, 45° bends and round stop symbols. I don’t need InDesign for that, and I couldn’t find a simple replacement. So I built one.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;It’s called Liniennetz-Editor, it’s free and open source (MIT), and it runs completely in the browser with no backend. Here’s how it works and what turned out to be tricky.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  The idea: Describe, not draw
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Graphics programs make you draw every line segment. For a network with 50 lines and 300 stations that is miserable. The editor flips this around:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ol&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Describe the network: stops, lines, categories (e.g. “frequent” vs. “rare”), which line serves which stops&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Place the stops on a grid&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The program computes everything else: connections, corners, parallel lanes, stop symbols, key&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The result is a modern-looking map that only uses 0°, 45° and 90°, exported as SVG, PNG or PDF.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  Stack
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;React and Fluent UI for the surrounding interface&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Every edit clones the project state, which gives undo/redo almost for free&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The map itself is plain SVG generated as a string in a separate engine module with no UI dependency&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Projects are saved as JSON files, no server involved&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Keeping the engine separate from the UI was the best early decision. The same function renders the interactive canvas and the export.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;


  1. Routing between two grid points
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Between two stops on a grid there are three cases: same row or column, exactly diagonal, or neither. The third case is the interesting one. You need a diagonal part of length &lt;code&gt;min(|dx|, |dy|)&lt;/code&gt; plus a straight part for the rest.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Where the straight part goes matters visually. Putting it all at one end looks clumsy, so I split it between both ends and let the diagonal sit in the middle:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight javascript"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="kd"&gt;function&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;route&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;a&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;b&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;dx&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;b&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;x&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;-&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;a&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;x&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;dy&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;b&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;y&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;-&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;a&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;y&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;ax&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nb"&gt;Math&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;abs&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;dx&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;ay&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nb"&gt;Math&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;abs&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;dy&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="k"&gt;if&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;!&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;ax&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;||&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;!&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;ay&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;||&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;ax&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;===&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;ay&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;return&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;a&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;b&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;]&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;      &lt;span class="c1"&gt;// straight or pure diagonal&lt;/span&gt;

  &lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;d&lt;/span&gt;  &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nb"&gt;Math&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;min&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;ax&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;ay&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;                      &lt;span class="c1"&gt;// diagonal length&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;n&lt;/span&gt;  &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nb"&gt;Math&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;abs&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;ax&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;-&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;ay&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;                     &lt;span class="c1"&gt;// straight remainder&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;n1&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nb"&gt;Math&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;ceil&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;n&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;/&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="mi"&gt;2&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;                      &lt;span class="c1"&gt;// straight part at the start&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;sx&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nb"&gt;Math&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;sign&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;dx&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;sy&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nb"&gt;Math&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;sign&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;dy&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;horizontal&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;ax&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;ay&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;

  &lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;p1&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;x&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;a&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;x&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;+&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;horizontal&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;?&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;sx&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;*&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;n1&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="mi"&gt;0&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
               &lt;span class="n"&gt;y&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;a&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;y&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;+&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;horizontal&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;?&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="mi"&gt;0&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;sy&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;*&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;n1&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;p2&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;x&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;p1&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;x&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;+&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;sx&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;*&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;d&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;y&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;p1&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;y&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;+&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;sy&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;*&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;d&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="k"&gt;return&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;a&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;p1&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;p2&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;b&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;]&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;The real version also handles odd remainders (a flip toggle lets the user choose which end gets the larger part) and removes degenerate points.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;One design rule matters a lot: routes are computed per edge, not per line. If two lines share a section, they automatically share the same geometry, which makes bundling possible later.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;


  2. Rounded corners
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Corners are replaced with circular arcs. The tangent length depends on the turning angle, and the radius is clamped so arcs never overlap on short segments:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight javascript"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="kd"&gt;function&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;fillet&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;a&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;v&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;b&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;r&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;l1&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nb"&gt;Math&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;hypot&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;v&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;x&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;-&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;a&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;x&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;v&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;y&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;-&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;a&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;y&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;l2&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nb"&gt;Math&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;hypot&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;b&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;x&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;-&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;v&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;x&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;b&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;y&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;-&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;v&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;y&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;u1&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;x&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;v&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;x&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;-&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;a&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;x&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;/&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;l1&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;y&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;v&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;y&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;-&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;a&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;y&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;/&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;l1&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;u2&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;x&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;b&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;x&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;-&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;v&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;x&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;/&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;l2&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;y&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;b&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;y&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;-&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;v&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;y&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;/&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;l2&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;

  &lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;theta&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nb"&gt;Math&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;acos&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;u1&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;x&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;*&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;u2&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;x&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;+&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;u1&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;y&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;*&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;u2&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;y&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;  &lt;span class="c1"&gt;// turning angle&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;k&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nb"&gt;Math&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;tan&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;theta&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;/&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="mi"&gt;2&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;t&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nb"&gt;Math&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;min&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;r&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;*&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;k&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;l1&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;/&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="mi"&gt;2&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;l2&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;/&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="mi"&gt;2&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;           &lt;span class="c1"&gt;// tangent length, clamped&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;rr&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;t&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;/&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;k&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;                                    &lt;span class="c1"&gt;// effective radius&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;sweep&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;u1&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;x&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;*&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;u2&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;y&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;-&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;u1&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;y&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;*&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;u2&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;x&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="mi"&gt;0&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;?&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="mi"&gt;1&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="mi"&gt;0&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;

  &lt;span class="k"&gt;return&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="sb"&gt;`L${v.x - u1.x * t} ${v.y - u1.y * t}`&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;+&lt;/span&gt;
         &lt;span class="sb"&gt;`A${rr} ${rr} 0 0 ${sweep} ${v.x + u2.x * t} ${v.y + u2.y * t}`&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;That string goes straight into an SVG &lt;code&gt;&amp;lt;path d="..."&amp;gt;&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;


  3. The hard part: bundling parallel lines
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;When three lines run along the same track, they should appear as three parallel strokes with a constant gap, including through bends.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;My approach:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Break every line into unit grid steps. Each step gets a key (its two endpoints).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;For each step, collect all lines that use it. Each line’s lane is its index in that list, centered: &lt;code&gt;offset = (index - (count - 1) / 2) * gap&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;At every vertex, compute the offset path’s corner by intersecting the two offset lines. That keeps the gap constant through a bend.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;For radii, give the innermost line the base radius and let the outer lines run concentrically around it, so strokes don’t cross inside a curve.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The nastiest bug class here is lane order. If two lines share a stretch, they must keep the same relative order along the whole shared run, otherwise they cross each other for no reason. The engine decides the order once per contiguous shared run, using the geometry (which side each line turns toward) as the tiebreaker. Users can override the order per connection by clicking it.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Where a lane count changes (a line joins or leaves a bundle), the path needs a 45° shift so the gap is preserved. Currently the whole bundle re-centers when that happens, which creates a visible kink in otherwise straight lines. A Reddit user rightly pointed out that straightness should beat symmetry here, so that’s next on my list.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;


  4. Stop symbols
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;A stop served by one line is a circle. A stop served by several parallel lines becomes a pill spanning all lanes, oriented across the bundle direction (including diagonals). If lines cross at different angles, the symbol turns into a rounded rectangle. Stops where only some lines call get a gap in the pill, drawn as separate parts joined by a thin connector.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;


  5. Performance
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;With about 300 stops and 50 lines, recomputing everything on each mouse move would be slow. A cheap fix works well: the engine builds a cache key from the relevant parts of the state and returns the previous result if nothing that affects geometry has changed. Dragging a label doesn’t recompute the routing.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;


  What I’d do differently
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Add automated tests for the geometry earlier. I verified the routing visually, which doesn’t scale.&lt;br&gt;
Decide on the data model for lane order from day one instead of retrofitting manual overrides.&lt;/p&gt;

